{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Yehoshua answered, etc., restrain them.</b> One needs to know on what basis Yehoshua presumed to render a ruling in the presence of his master — and all the more so to instruct him, כֹּה וְכֹה תַּעֲשֶׂה (״thus and thus shall you do״) — which is a sign of presumptuousness. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Eruvin 63a): anyone who offers a ruling in the presence of his master departs childless, as it is said: ״וַיַּעַן יְהוֹשֻׁעַ״ etc. And it is possible to give a reason for Yehoshua's action according to their words of blessed memory (Sifrei), which state as follows: What prophecy did they prophesy? Moshe dies, Yehoshua brings them in — end of quotation. Therefore, when Yehoshua heard these things, he chose to speak in the presence of his master in order to reveal his view that the words were repugnant to him and to those who spoke them, and that falsehood was in their mouths. And by this he removed the suspicion that he desired the things said regarding his advancement, and he revealed the very opposite in his intent." "<b>And he said,</b> my master Moshe, <b>restrain them</b> — meaning, place them under guard until a royal decree of judgment arrives, or obliterate them from the world. And the reason for this holds whether according to the view that they were from outside the seventy or according to the view that they were from among the seventy, for the reasons we have written. And perhaps he alluded by saying <b>my master Moshe</b>, that he had no desire to be master himself but rather that his master should be Moshe — to negate the desire implied in what was said, that Moshe would die and he would bring them in. And it may also be inferred from the word <b>וַיַּעַן</b> (״and he answered״) that he gave a reply to the things spoken against him in that prophecy, for they did not speak truthfully and deserved to be put in prison. Even so, Scripture punished him, for in the end he issued a ruling in the presence of his master (I Chronicles 7:27)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:57.000420478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}